A CNI plugin that gives FreeBSD containers an address on a real LAN segment.

FreeBSD has no macvlan. This plugin does the native equivalent: it creates an
epair per container, attaches one end to a host bridge, moves the other into
the container's jail, and applies the address supplied by IPAM.

It implements the ADD, DEL, CHECK and VERSION commands, and delegates address
allocation to the IPAM plugin named in the network configuration.
